      "body": "#### Summary\n\nThe `GaugeManager` contract contains a critical flaw where emissions notified when `totalWeight` is zero are transferred into the contract but never allocated to gauges. This occurs because the `notifyRewardAmount` function transfers tokens but sets the ratio to zero when totalWeight is zero, preventing any index updates that would enable future distribution of these emissions.\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen `notifyRewardAmount()` is called while `IVoter(voter).totalWeight()` returns zero, the function transfers base tokens from the minter into GaugeManager but fails to update the global index properly. The emission accounting logic computes a ratio of zero when totalWeight is zero, resulting in no index increment. Since gauge distributions rely entirely on index deltas to calculate claimable amounts, these transferred tokens become permanently inaccessible.\n\nThe vulnerable flow occurs in the notification process where totalWeight can legitimately be zero during early protocol operation or when voting weights temporarily drop to zero. The contract transfers the emission tokens but creates no mechanism to track or redistribute them once voting weight is restored. The `_updateForAfterDistribution()` function only processes index deltas, so previously unaccounted emissions remain stranded indefinitely.\n\n#### Affected Code\n\n`ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol:268-280`\n\n```solidity\nfunction notifyRewardAmount(uint256 amount) external {\n    require(msg.sender == minter, \"NA\");\n    IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n\n    uint256 _ratio = 0;\n    uint256 totalWeight = IVoter(voter).totalWeight();\n    if(totalWeight > 0) _ratio = amount * 1e18 / Math.max(totalWeight, 1);     // 1e18 adjustment is removed during claim\n    if (_ratio > 0) {\n        index += _ratio;\n    }\n\n    emit NotifyReward(msg.sender, base, amount);\n}\n```\n\n`ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol:371-395`\n\n```solidity\n/// @notice update info for gauges\n/// @dev    this function track the gauge index to emit the correct $the amount after the distribution\nfunction _updateForAfterDistribution(address _gauge) private {\n    address _pool = poolForGauge[_gauge];\n    //uint256 _supplied = weightsPerEpoch[_time][_pool];\n    uint256 _supplied = IVoter(voter).weights(_pool);\n\n    if (_supplied > 0) {\n        uint256 _supplyIndex = supplyIndex[_gauge];\n        uint256 _index = index; // get global index0 for accumulated distro\n        // SupplyIndex will be updated for Killed Gauges as well so we don't need to udpate index while reviving gauge.\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = _index; // update _gauge current position to global position\n        uint256 _delta = _index - _supplyIndex; // see if there is any difference that need to be accrued\n        if (_delta > 0) {\n            uint256 _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18; // add accrued difference for each supplied token\n            if (isAlive[_gauge]) {\n                claimable[_gauge] += _share;\n            } else {\n                IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransfer(minter, _share); // send rewards back to Minter so they're not stuck in GaugeManager\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = index; // new users are set to the default global state\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\n#### Impact Explanation\n\nThis vulnerability causes permanent loss of scheduled emissions intended for distribution to users. When totalWeight is zero during emission notification, the transferred tokens remain in GaugeManager indefinitely with no recovery mechanism. This breaks the emission distribution policy and creates unclaimable funds, undermining the protocol's token economics and causing direct financial losses to stakeholders expecting those emissions.\n\n#### Likelihood Explanation\n\nThe vulnerability has medium likelihood as zero-weight epochs are realistic scenarios, particularly at protocol genesis before any votes are cast or during operational periods when voting weight temporarily drops to zero. Since emission notification occurs as part of regular epoch rollover without requiring special privileges, this condition can arise under normal operation sequencing, especially during protocol launch phases.\n\n#### Recommendation\n\nConsider implementing a pending emission mechanism to handle notifications when totalWeight is zero. One approach could be to track unallocated emissions in a separate variable when totalWeight is zero, then incorporate these pending amounts into the index calculation once totalWeight becomes positive. This would ensure that all notified emissions eventually reach their intended recipients regardless of timing.\n\nAlternatively, the notification function could be modified to either reject emissions when totalWeight is zero or defer the transfer until voting weight is established, preventing the accumulation of stranded tokens while maintaining emission schedule integrity.\n**Impact:** The proof of concept demonstrates that when `GaugeManager.notifyRewardAmount` is called while `IVoter(voter).totalWeight() == 0`, the full epoch emission is transferred into `GaugeManager` but does not increase the global index, leaving those tokens untracked. After votes are cast in the next epoch and distributions proceed, the newly minted emission is distributed to the gauge, while the previous epoch's tokens remain stuck in `GaugeManager` (balance does not decrease), proving passive value loss and permanently stranded emissions.",
      "proofOfConcept": "#### Proof of Concept\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"../C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\n\n// Minimal ERC20 for pairing (top-level contract; simple and local to test)\ncontract MockERC20 {\n        string public name;\n        string public symbol;\n        uint8 public decimals;\n        uint public totalSupply;\n        mapping(address => uint) public balanceOf;\n        mapping(address => mapping(address => uint)) public allowance;\n\n        event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint value);\n        event Approval(address indexed owner, address indexed spender, uint value);\n\n        constructor(string memory _name, string memory _symbol, uint8 _decimals) {\n            name = _name;\n            symbol = _symbol;\n            decimals = _decimals;\n        }\n\n        function _mint(address to, uint amount) external {\n            totalSupply += amount;\n            balanceOf[to] += amount;\n            emit Transfer(address(0), to, amount);\n        }\n\n        function approve(address spender, uint value) external returns (bool) {\n            allowance[msg.sender][spender] = value;\n            emit Approval(msg.sender, spender, value);\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        function transfer(address to, uint value) external returns (bool) {\n            return _transfer(msg.sender, to, value);\n        }\n\n        function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint value) external returns (bool) {\n            uint allowed = allowance[from][msg.sender];\n            if (allowed != type(uint).max) {\n                require(allowed >= value, \"allowance\");\n                allowance[from][msg.sender] = allowed - value;\n            }\n            return _transfer(from, to, value);\n        }\n\n        function _transfer(address from, address to, uint value) internal returns (bool) {\n            require(balanceOf[from] >= value, \"balance\");\n            balanceOf[from] -= value;\n            balanceOf[to] += value;\n            emit Transfer(from, to, value);\n            return true;\n        }\n}\n\ncontract GM_NotifyZeroWeight_Stuck is C4PoCTestbed {\n\n    address public pool;\n    address public gauge;\n    MockERC20 public other;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Initialize BribeFactoryV3 so GaugeManager can create bribes\n        bribeFactoryV3.initialize(address(voter), address(gaugeManager), address(permissionsRegistry), address(tokenHandler));\n\n        // Give this test contract governance so we can whitelist tokens/connectors\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GOVERNANCE\");\n\n        // Deploy a second ERC20 to pair with HYBR and whitelist both\n        other = new MockERC20(\"OTHER\", \"OTR\", 18);\n        tokenHandler.whitelistToken(address(hybr));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistToken(address(other));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(hybr));\n\n        // Create a vAMM pair (Thena mock) and a gauge for it\n        pool = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(hybr), address(other), false);\n        (gauge,,) = gaugeManager.createGauge(pool, 0);\n\n        // Sanity: no votes yet\n        assertEq(voter.totalWeight(), 0, \"pre: totalWeight should be zero\");\n    }\n\n    function test_stuckEmissions_whenNotifyAtZeroWeight() public {\n        // 1) First epoch emission while totalWeight == 0\n        // Advance to next epoch and trigger mint + notify\n        uint WEEK = minter.WEEK();\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + WEEK + 1);\n        gaugeManager.distributeAll();\n\n        // Emissions transferred into GaugeManager, but index not increased (totalWeight==0)\n        uint gmBalAfterFirst = hybr.balanceOf(address(gaugeManager));\n        assertGt(gmBalAfterFirst, 0, \"gaugeManager should hold stranded emissions after first notify\");\n        // No distribution should have happened (no claimable without index delta)\n        assertEq(hybr.balanceOf(gauge), 0, \"gauge must not receive rewards in first epoch\");\n\n        // 2) Create voting power and vote for the pool\n        uint lockAmt = 1_000_000 ether;\n        hybr.approve(address(votingEscrow), lockAmt);\n        uint tokenId = votingEscrow.create_lock(lockAmt, 365 days);\n\n        // Move to a safe time inside the voting window to avoid DW revert\n        // Voting is only allowed after epochStart + NO_VOTING_WINDOW (300s)\n        uint __WEEK = minter.WEEK();\n        uint start = block.timestamp - (block.timestamp % __WEEK);\n        uint voteStart = start + 300; // NO_VOTING_WINDOW\n        if (block.timestamp <= voteStart) {\n            vm.warp(voteStart + 1);\n        }\n        address[] memory pools = new address[](1);\n        pools[0] = pool;\n        uint[] memory weights = new uint[](1);\n        weights[0] = 10000;\n        voter.vote(tokenId, pools, weights);\n        assertGt(voter.totalWeight(), 0, \"post: totalWeight should be > 0 after voting\");\n\n        // 3) Second epoch emission with nonzero totalWeight; should be distributed to the gauge\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + WEEK + 1);\n        gaugeManager.distributeAll();\n\n        // Gauge should now have received rewards from the second epoch\n        uint gaugeReceived = hybr.balanceOf(gauge);\n        assertGt(gaugeReceived, 0, \"gauge should receive second epoch rewards\");\n\n        // Critically, the first epoch emissions remain stuck in GaugeManager forever\n        // Balance should remain at least the same (may grow slightly due to rounding residues in later epochs)\n        uint gmBalAfterSecond = hybr.balanceOf(address(gaugeManager));\n        assertGe(gmBalAfterSecond, gmBalAfterFirst, \"GaugeManager balance should not decrease; stranded emissions persist\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Command:** `cd ve33 && forge test -vvv --match-path test/poc/GM_NotifyZeroWeight_Stuck.t.sol`",
